# next-auth@4's package.json declares peerDependencies
# next: "^12.2.5 || ^13 || ^14 || ^15" — it does not yet list Next.js 16,
# even though it works fine with it in practice (confirmed by the
# Next.js/next-auth community as of this migration). Without this,
# `npm install` fails outright with an unresolvable peer dependency
# conflict. Auth.js v5 (the next-auth major that officially supports
# Next 16) is still in beta, so it isn't used here — see README.
#
# Remove this file once next-auth publishes a release with an updated
# peerDependencies range for Next.js 16, at which point plain
# `npm install` will work without it.
legacy-peer-deps=true
